    {
      "id": "03-open",
      "instruction": "In the Ghost admin, open the post titled '{{runid}} Bench Post' (its editor is at {{02-create.url}}) and open its settings panel (the post settings sidebar). In the settings panel do three things: (1) In the tags field, type 'Bench News' and choose the EXISTING tag 'Bench News' from the suggestion dropdown — do NOT create a new tag, and be careful not to pick the similarly named existing tag 'Bench Newsletter'; the post's only tag must end up being the existing 'Bench News'. (2) In the custom excerpt field, set the excerpt to text that includes the string '{{runid}}' (e.g. 'Bench post for run {{runid}}.'). (3) Set the publish date to 2026-09-01 (September 1, 2026), keeping the time as whatever the app offers. Save/close the settings and wait for the post to be saved. Do NOT publish the post yet. Then report exactly: the tags shown in the settings panel, the excerpt text shown, the publish date shown, and the URL slug shown in the settings panel, plus the post's current status indicator.",
      "skill": "s_593303",
      "params": {
        "v1": "{{runid}} Bench Post",
        "v3": "{{02-create.url.h2}}",
        "v2": "{{runid}}",
        "v4": "Bench post for run {{runid}}.",
